The RTMP modules turn nginx into a streaming server: they take a live
stream in over RTMP, relay it to other servers, record it, and serve it
again as HLS or MPEG-DASH.  A statistics and a control endpoint are
served over HTTP, and an external program such as ffmpeg can be run per
stream to transcode it.

This port only installs the module sources.  The modules themselves are
built by the nginx ports when their RTMP option is enabled.
